# Template for the GitHub MCP token. Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in your own value.
#
# IMPORTANT: Claude Code does NOT auto-load .env files. Copying this to .env is not enough on
# its own — .mcp.json expands ${GITHUB_MCP_TOKEN} from the *process environment* of the Claude
# Code process, so the variable must reach that environment before the client starts. Three
# verified ways to do that (see HOWTORUN.md section 4.1):
#
#   1. Source this file into the launching shell:
#        cd homework-5 && set -a && . ./.env && set +a && claude
#   2. Put it in homework-5/.claude/settings.local.json under an "env" key (git-ignored,
#      persists across launches, no per-launch step).
#   3. Export it directly, without using .env at all:
#        export GITHUB_MCP_TOKEN=$(gh auth token)
#
# If the variable never reaches the environment, `claude mcp list` reports:
#   [Warning] [github] mcpServers.github: Missing environment variables: GITHUB_MCP_TOKEN
#   github: ... ✘ Failed to connect — HTTP 400: ... Authorization header is badly formatted
#
# Minimum scope needed (this homework only reads a public repo):
#     classic PAT      -> public_repo
#     fine-grained PAT -> Metadata: Read (mandatory), Pull requests: Read,
#                         Issues: Read, Contents: Read
#
# The connection also sends X-MCP-Readonly: true, so no write tool is ever offered.
GITHUB_MCP_TOKEN=ghp_replace_with_your_own_token
